from lesson_helpers import example as ex
DATA={
'sha':'972d7cd71d985f0c67970690923f0079c49ee28b','colour':'#127c83','first':'BoundedMeasurement',
'subtitle':('把不确定假设写清楚：区间、候选、约束与响应解释','Make uncertain assumptions explicit: intervals, candidates, constraints and response interpretation'),
'intro':[
('UncertaintyLibrary 处理确定性有界假设：公差、初始状态范围、标定误差、模型差异和给定响应的比较。它既有区间与候选构造函数，也有可接线的扰动模块及依赖明确假设的解析界函数。','UncertaintyLibrary handles deterministic bounded assumptions: tolerances, initial-state ranges, calibration errors, model discrepancy and comparisons of supplied responses. It includes interval and candidate functions, connected perturbation blocks and analytical bounds conditional on explicit assumptions.'),
('本库不会自动把候选点变成一批仿真，也不会为区间自动分配概率。用户必须说明候选如何驱动本体、结果从何而来，以及结论覆盖的是有限点、采样轨迹，还是在额外数学条件下成立的区间界。','The library does not automatically turn candidates into a simulation campaign or assign probabilities to intervals. Explain how candidates drive the host, where responses originate, and whether conclusions cover finite points, sampled trajectories or interval bounds under additional mathematical conditions.')],
'route':[
('运行 BoundedMeasurement，理解区间与一个选定取值不是同一个对象。','Run BoundedMeasurement and distinguish an interval from one selected value.'),
('学习 ToleranceAndSelection 与 IntervalArithmetic，手算端点并核对符号。','Study ToleranceAndSelection and IntervalArithmetic, calculating endpoints and checking signs by hand.'),
('学习网格、共享坐标与可行性筛选，再建立自己的候选—本体映射。','Study grids, shared coordinates and feasibility filtering, then define your own candidate-to-host mapping.'),
('最后解释包络、有限最差值和灵敏度，明确每一种结论的覆盖边界。','Finally interpret envelopes, finite observed worst values and sensitivity, stating the scope of each conclusion.')],
'concepts':[
(('区间表示范围，不表示概率分布','An interval is a range, not a probability distribution'),'Sets.Interval(lo,hi) 表示有序闭区间。区间没有内置均匀分布、置信水平或失效率；中点只是选定代表值，不是由数据估计的期望。单位和物理含义由调用者维护。','Sets.Interval(lo,hi) represents an ordered closed interval. It supplies no uniform distribution, confidence level or failure rate. Its midpoint is a selected representative, not a data-estimated expectation. The caller owns units and physical meaning.'),
(('坐标是可复现的选择规则','A coordinate is a reproducible selection rule'),'SelectPoint 把 xi∈[-1,1] 映射到区间，-1/0/1 分别选下端、中点、上端。useCoordinateInput=false 时使用参数 xi；启用后必须连接 coordinate。时间变化坐标是显式时变输入，不是自动抽样。','SelectPoint maps xi in [-1,1] into the interval; -1, 0 and 1 select lower, midpoint and upper values. With useCoordinateInput=false the parameter xi is used; otherwise connect coordinate. A time-varying coordinate is an explicit signal, not automatic sampling.'),
(('候选构造、仿真执行与响应分析是三个步骤','Candidate construction, execution and analysis are separate'),'Grid1D、BoxCorners、CartesianGrid 只生成数值。研究者决定把这些值绑定到参数后分别仿真，或在一个模型中实例化多个本体；Analysis 处理提供的响应，不替用户补做未运行工况。','Grid1D, BoxCorners and CartesianGrid generate values. The researcher binds them to separate runs or multiple host instances. Analysis operates on supplied responses; it does not execute unperformed cases.'),
(('共享坐标是依赖假设，不是统计相关估计','A shared coordinate imposes dependence, not estimated correlation'),'SharedCoordinate 和 AffineCoordinateMap 让多项量随共同坐标变化，可以避免把物理上联动的参数任意组合。但这是一种人为选择的依赖结构，不能说它已经从数据识别了相关系数。','SharedCoordinate and AffineCoordinateMap vary quantities through common coordinates and can prevent arbitrary combinations of linked parameters. This imposes a chosen dependency structure; it does not estimate a correlation coefficient from data.'),
(('观测最差值与有条件解析界不同','Observed extrema and conditional analytical bounds differ'),'有限候选的最大值只覆盖已提供样本；EnvelopeAtSamples 只覆盖同一网格上的已有轨迹。LipschitzEnvelope 或 InterpolationErrorBounds 的结论依赖用户给定的全域导数界等条件。区间算术使用普通浮点数，并非自动提供定向舍入的严格计算证明。','A finite maximum covers supplied candidates; EnvelopeAtSamples covers supplied trajectories on a common grid. LipschitzEnvelope and InterpolationErrorBounds depend on user-supplied global derivative bounds or related conditions. Interval arithmetic uses ordinary floating point rather than automatically furnishing a directed-rounding proof.')],
'groups':[
('Sets',('区间、公差与物理状态范围','Intervals, tolerances and physical-state ranges'),'先定义区间端点、单位及依据；用绝对/相对公差构造，或调用加减乘除、交并包络、非对称公差和物理储能界。Divide 的分母不得跨零；不要通过排序错误输入掩盖物理不一致。','Declare endpoints, units and justification first. Construct tolerances or use arithmetic, intersection/hull, asymmetric tolerances and physical-energy bounds. Divide requires a denominator excluding zero; do not hide physically inconsistent inputs by silently reordering them.'),
('Candidates',('有限候选集合','Finite candidate sets'),'选择一维网格、盒角点或笛卡尔网格，记录点数与行顺序。单点轴取中点，笛卡尔网格最后一维变化最快；上限防止意外构造过大数组。候选必须再绑定到本体执行。','Choose a one-dimensional grid, box corners or Cartesian grid and record count and row ordering. A singleton axis uses its midpoint, and the last Cartesian dimension varies fastest. Capacity bounds prevent accidental oversized arrays. Bind candidates to host executions separately.'),
('Constraints',('可行性约束','Feasibility constraints'),'用 BoxFeasibility 或 LinearFeasibility 检查明确的约束，再筛选候选。FilterCandidates 保留固定数组，用掩码和有效索引表达筛选；只读取前 nAccepted 个索引，并检查 available。','Apply declared box or linear constraints and then filter candidates. FilterCandidates preserves fixed-size arrays and returns masks and valid indices. Read only the first nAccepted indices and inspect available.'),
('Perturbations',('有界信号与标定误差','Bounded signal and calibration errors'),'把 u 接到名义信号，把 y 接到实际接收端；设置 range、xi 或 coordinate。加性误差与比例误差单位不同，标定增益和零点可使用独立或共享坐标；lower/upper 是该模块的明确局部关系，不自动成为闭环响应界。','Connect u to the nominal signal and y to the receiver, then configure range and xi or coordinate. Additive and relative gain errors have different units; calibration gain and offset may use separate or shared coordinates. Local lower/upper outputs do not automatically bound the complete closed-loop response.'),
('Analysis',('响应分析与有条件的界','Response analysis and conditional bounds'),'传入已有响应、候选或导数界；确认方向、单位、有效性和样本网格。有限差分要求一致的正负扰动与步长；归一化灵敏度必须检查参考分母；解析范围类的先决条件要有独立依据。','Supply responses, candidates or derivative bounds and establish direction, units, validity and sample-grid alignment. Finite differences require consistent perturbations and step size. Check the reference denominator before normalisation and independently justify analytical-bound assumptions.')],
'examples':{
'BoundedMeasurement':ex(('选定加性与比例误差','Selected additive and relative gain errors'),('误差区间怎样变成当前仿真中的一个明确值？','How does an error interval become one explicit value in a simulation?'),('名义输入 10，coordinate 在 1 s 和 2 s 从 -1 切到 0 再到 1。加性区间 [-0.2,0.2]，相对增益区间 [-0.02,0.02]。','Nominal input is 10. coordinate changes from -1 to 0 at 1 s and to 1 at 2 s. The additive interval is [-0.2,0.2] and relative gain interval [-0.02,0.02].'),('两个输出在当前名义值下都依次为 9.8、10、10.2。二者数值碰巧相同，不代表两种误差模型对任意输入等价。','Both outputs are 9.8, 10 and 10.2 in sequence for this nominal value. This numerical agreement does not make the two error models equivalent for every input.'),['coordinate.y','additiveValue','gainValue','additive.delta','additive.lower','additive.upper'],('把 nominal.k 改为 20：加性误差幅度仍为 0.2，而比例误差的绝对幅度变为 0.4。','Change nominal.k to 20: additive magnitude remains 0.2 while the absolute gain-error magnitude becomes 0.4.'),('这个坐标序列是指定轨迹，不是三个独立随机样本。','This coordinate sequence is prescribed, not three independent random samples.')),
'ToleranceAndSelection':ex(('公差端点与代表点','Tolerance endpoints and representative points'),('负中心值的相对公差应如何计算？','How should relative tolerance be constructed around a negative centre?'),('辅助视图计算中心 -10 的 10% 相对公差，以及中心 2 的 0.1 绝对公差，并选择下端、中点和上端。','The helper constructs 10% relative tolerance around -10 and absolute tolerance 0.1 around 2, then selects lower, midpoint and upper values.'),('relativeLo=-11、relativeHi=-9；绝对公差区间为 [1.9,2.1]，mid=2。相对公差使用中心值的幅值，因此端点不会倒置。','relativeLo=-11 and relativeHi=-9. The absolute interval is [1.9,2.1] with mid=2. Relative tolerance uses the centre magnitude, preventing reversed endpoints.'),['relativeLo','relativeHi','absoluteLo','mid','absoluteHi'],('改用非对称公差函数，比较中心值不再必然等于区间中点的情况。','Use an asymmetric tolerance function and compare cases where the nominal centre is no longer the interval midpoint.'),('端点与中点只是选择方案；没有覆盖全部连续区间的仿真。','Endpoint and midpoint selection does not simulate the entire continuous interval.')),
'IntervalArithmetic':ex(('区间四则运算与负比例映射','Interval arithmetic and negative affine scaling'),('怎样避免只按相同位置端点相乘而漏掉极值？','How can interval arithmetic avoid missing extrema by pairing only corresponding endpoints?'),('使用 a=[-2,3] 与 b=[4,5] 计算加、减、乘、除，再对 a 应用 -2a+1。','Use a=[-2,3] and b=[4,5] for addition, subtraction, multiplication and division, then apply -2a+1.'),('结果依次为 [2,8]、[-7,-1]、[-10,15]、[-0.5,0.75] 和 [-5,5]。乘除必须考虑符号与所有端点组合；负比例会反转端点顺序。','The results are [2,8], [-7,-1], [-10,15], [-0.5,0.75] and [-5,5]. Multiplication/division require sign-aware endpoint combinations; negative scaling reverses endpoint order.'),['sumLower','sumUpper','differenceLower','differenceUpper','productLower','productUpper','ratioLower','ratioUpper','mappedLower','mappedUpper'],('将分母区间改为跨零区间，检查先决条件报错，而不是接受一个伪有限结果。','Change the denominator to an interval containing zero and inspect the precondition failure rather than accepting a fictitious finite result.'),('重复使用同一不确定量可能产生依赖过估计，例如 x-x 不一定由独立区间运算直接得到零。','Repeated occurrences of one uncertain quantity can produce dependency overestimation; independent interval arithmetic need not reduce x-x to zero.')),
'CandidateGrids':ex(('角点、网格与单点轴','Corners, grids and singleton axes'),('不同候选构造方法给出多少点，顺序如何？','How many points do candidate schemes produce, and in what order?'),('对二维盒 [0,2]×[-1,1] 比较全部角点与每轴三点的网格；另对 [0,2] 构造一维单点网格。','Compare all corners of [0,2]×[-1,1] with a three-point-per-axis grid and construct a singleton one-dimensional grid on [0,2].'),('corners=4、gridPoints=9、singleton=1；最后一维变化最快，因此 secondCornerY=1，中央网格点的 middleX=1。','corners=4, gridPoints=9 and singleton=1. The last dimension varies fastest, giving secondCornerY=1 and middleX=1 for the central grid point.'),['corners','gridPoints','singleton','secondCornerY','middleX'],('把一轴改为单点，核对它固定在中点而不是下端点；增加维度前先计算候选总数。','Make one axis a singleton and check that it uses the midpoint, not the lower endpoint. Calculate total count before increasing dimensionality.'),('网格大小随维数增长；CartesianGrid 的规模限制不是全局优化算法。','Grid size grows with dimension. The CartesianGrid capacity limit is not a global optimisation algorithm.')),
'CoupledAndConstrainedCandidates':ex(('可行性筛选与共同变化','Feasibility filtering and shared variation'),('如何排除违反工程约束的组合，又如何表达参数联动？','How can infeasible combinations be removed and linked variation represented?'),('对 {0,1,2}² 的候选施加 x+y≤2；另一部分使用中心 {2,5}、半径 {0.1,0.3} 和公共坐标 -1、0、1。','Filter {0,1,2}² by x+y≤2. A separate part uses centre {2,5}, radii {0.1,0.3} and a shared coordinate -1, 0 or 1.'),('acceptedCount=6；被观察的第二个共享量分别为 4.7、5、5.3。筛选索引只在前 nAccepted 项有意义。','acceptedCount=6. The observed second shared quantity is 4.7, 5 and 5.3. Only the first nAccepted entries of the returned index array are meaningful.'),['acceptedCount','sharedLower','sharedMiddle','sharedUpper'],('收紧约束至没有可行点，检查 available 与计数；不要把填充索引当作候选一。','Tighten the constraint until no points remain and inspect availability and count; do not interpret padding indices as valid candidates.'),('共享坐标只是声明依赖，并不估计概率相关系数。','A shared coordinate declares dependence; it does not estimate statistical correlation.')),
'InitialConditionEnvelope':ex(('三种初态的公共网格包络','Common-grid envelope of three initial states'),('已有轨迹如何形成可复现的响应范围？','How can existing trajectories form a reproducible response envelope?'),('三个 T=0.5 的一阶本体接受零输入，初值分别 -0.1、0、0.1；每 0.1 s 采样一次并计算下上界。','Three first-order hosts with T=0.5 receive zero input and start at -0.1, 0 and 0.1. They are sampled every 0.1 s to calculate lower and upper values.'),('在采样时刻，理论包络为 ±0.1 exp(-2t)，nValid=3；显示中的区间间隔可能保持上次样本，不代表连续时间之间所有细节都已计算。','At sample instants the analytical envelope is ±0.1 exp(-2t), with nValid=3. Held values between samples do not mean that all intervening continuous-time behaviour was evaluated.'),['run1.y','run2.y','run3.y','lower','upper','nValid'],('改变一个本体的 T，再检查包络是否仍能用同一解析式描述；保持采样网格一致。','Change T for one host and check whether the same analytical expression still applies, retaining an aligned sample grid.'),('这里覆盖三个已连接的本体，不自动证明任何额外初态或参数组合。','The envelope covers the three connected hosts, not arbitrary additional initial states or parameter combinations.')),
'FiniteCandidateWorstCase':ex(('加入内部候选改变观测最大值','An interior candidate changes the observed maximum'),('只试区间两端会不会漏掉更差的响应？','Can endpoint-only testing miss a more severe response?'),('对 f(p)=1-p² 比较 {-1,1} 与 {-1,0,1} 两组输入响应。','Compare f(p)=1-p² on {-1,1} and {-1,0,1}.'),('endpointMaximum=0，enrichedMaximum=1，enrichedIndex=2。内部候选使观测最大值增大，直接说明“只测两端”没有一般保证。','endpointMaximum=0, enrichedMaximum=1 and enrichedIndex=2. Adding an interior candidate raises the observed maximum, demonstrating that endpoint-only testing has no general guarantee.'),['endpointMaximum','enrichedMaximum','enrichedIndex'],('把响应函数改成单调函数，再比较两组结果；把数学单调性证明与有限观测单调性区分开。','Replace the response by a monotonic function and compare both sets, distinguishing a mathematical monotonicity proof from observed monotonicity.'),('本例已知二次函数可以额外解析证明极值，但 CandidateExtrema 本身只分析传入数值。','The known quadratic permits a separate analytical extremum proof; CandidateExtrema itself analyses supplied values only.')),
'LocalSensitivity':ex(('中心差分与归一化局部灵敏度','Central difference and normalised local sensitivity'),('怎样把正负扰动响应转成可解释的局部斜率？','How can positive and negative perturbations yield an interpretable local slope?'),('以 p=2 为中心、步长 0.001，对 p² 的响应进行中心差分，再按中心参数和名义响应归一化。','Use centre p=2 and step 0.001 for the response p², then normalise using the centre parameter and nominal response.'),('解析导数为 4，归一化值为 (2/4)×4=2，available 应为真。检查斜率单位和归一化分母，而不是只报告一个数字。','The analytical derivative is 4 and the normalised value is (2/4)×4=2, with available=true. Check slope units and the reference denominator before reporting the number.'),['slope','normalized','available'],('逐步增大和减小步长，观察截断误差、数值噪声与参考分母接近零时的资格变化。','Increase and decrease the step to examine truncation error, numerical noise and qualification near a zero reference denominator.'),('局部斜率不能代表大范围非线性，也不能自动排序所有相互耦合参数的重要性。','A local slope does not describe large-range nonlinearity or automatically rank all coupled parameters.') )
},
'study':[
('先写一张参数假设表：物理量、单位、名义值、上下界、边界依据以及依赖约束。再选择候选方案，运行相同本体和求解设置，最后把有效响应交给 Analysis。候选生成、执行成功和结果有效要分别记录。','Begin with an assumption table listing quantity, units, nominal value, bounds, justification and dependency constraints. Choose candidates, run the same host and solver settings, and supply qualified responses to Analysis. Record candidate construction, execution success and result validity separately.'),
('下方最小实验使用固定上端点 xi=1。把它改为 -1 或 0 可以形成三次可复现运行；也可以启用 coordinate 输入，但那代表同一运行中的时变误差，不能与三次独立固定参数实验混称。','The minimal experiment below selects the upper endpoint with xi=1. Changing it to -1 or 0 defines three reproducible runs. Enabling a coordinate input instead introduces a time-varying error within one run, which is a different experiment.')],
'snippet':'''within;
model MyBoundedMeasurement
  Modelica.Blocks.Sources.Constant nominal(k=10);
  UncertaintyLibrary.Perturbations.AdditiveBound error(
    useCoordinateInput=false, xi=1,
    range=UncertaintyLibrary.Sets.Interval(-0.2, 0.2));
equation
  connect(nominal.y, error.u);
  annotation(experiment(StopTime=1, Tolerance=1e-6));
end MyBoundedMeasurement;''',
 'trouble':[
(('候选已经生成，为什么没有仿真结果','Why are there no simulation results after creating candidates?'),'候选函数只返回参数数组。需要用户显式实例化本体或使用外部运行脚本，完成每个候选的仿真并保存响应；本库没有自动批处理调度器。','Candidate functions return parameter arrays only. Instantiate hosts or use an external runner to execute each case and retain responses; the library contains no automatic campaign scheduler.'),
(('没有可行候选却得到数值零','Why is zero returned when no candidate is feasible?'),'查看 available、nAccepted 和有效掩码。固定大小数组和数值字段可能含占位值；没有资格的占位零不是一个已测得的安全结果。','Inspect available, nAccepted and validity masks. Fixed-size arrays and numeric fields may contain placeholders; an unavailable zero is not an observed safe result.'),
(('包络输入轨迹的时间点不一致','The envelope trajectories use different time grids'),'先在外部建立明确、可审计的公共网格和插值规则。EnvelopeAtSamples 不会替用户自动修复错位轨迹；重采样本身也可能影响峰值。','Establish an explicit auditable common grid and interpolation rule externally. EnvelopeAtSamples does not automatically repair misaligned trajectories, and resampling can itself affect peaks.'),
(('可以把界称为置信区间吗','Can these bounds be called confidence intervals?'),'不能仅凭上下界这样表述。确定性范围、有限候选覆盖和统计置信区间有不同前提；报告时使用与实际证据一致的术语。','Not merely because lower and upper endpoints exist. Deterministic bounds, finite candidate coverage and statistical confidence intervals have different assumptions; use terminology matching the evidence.')]
}
